llm_calls.content:
{
  "selected_feature_id": 0,
  "rationale": "Age is one of the most stable predictors of health insurance coverage across states because eligibility and coverage mechanisms vary strongly over the life course, including dependence for children, labor-market attachment for working ages, and near-universal Medicare eligibility at older ages. It adds major signal beyond income and employment while being less likely than race, ancestry, citizenship, or state to encode brittle geographic or demographic shortcuts."
}

